          "name": "RigorFoundry",
          "rules": [
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A test double may replace the production boundary that the test claims to prove."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Test-double API or fixture signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** A test double may replace the production boundary that the test claims to prove.\n\n**How to verify.** Trace the test from its public API, CLI, adapter, or workflow entry point; verify that the substituted object is an approved protocol-faithful external fixture and that the production adapter and validation path still execute.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Test-double API or fixture signal.\n\nWhy it matters: A test double may replace the production boundary that the test claims to prove.\nHow to verify: Trace the test from its public API, CLI, adapter, or workflow entry point; verify that the substituted object is an approved protocol-faithful external fixture and that the production adapter and validation path still execute."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta001-test-double",
              "id": "TA001-test-double",
              "name": "TA001-test-double",
              "properties": {
                "category": "test-authenticity",
                "introduced": "rigor-foundry/1.0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "rigor-foundry",
                  "test-authenticity"
                ]
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "kinds": [
                    "subset"
                  ],
                  "target": {
                    "id": "test-authenticity",
                    "index": 0,
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "index": 0,
                      "name": "RigorFoundry rule categories"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Test-double API or fixture signal."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Synthetic naming can identify fixtures that do not represent a real contract."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Synthetic fake, stub, dummy, or toy naming signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** Synthetic naming can identify fixtures that do not represent a real contract.\n\n**How to verify.** Compare the fixture with the repository schema, external protocol, recorded artefact, or documented domain example and prove which production boundary consumes it.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Synthetic fake, stub, dummy, or toy naming signal.\n\nWhy it matters: Synthetic naming can identify fixtures that do not represent a real contract.\nHow to verify: Compare the fixture with the repository schema, external protocol, recorded artefact, or documented domain example and prove which production boundary consumes it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta002-synthetic-fixture",
              "id": "TA002-synthetic-fixture",
              "name": "TA002-synthetic-fixture",
              "properties": {
                "category": "test-authenticity",
                "introduced": "rigor-foundry/1.0.0",
                "tags": [
