                    "index": 0,
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "index": 0,
                      "name": "RigorFoundry rule categories"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Synthetic fake, stub, dummy, or toy naming signal."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A conditional or ignored test can hide an unverified production path."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Skipped or expected-failure test signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** A conditional or ignored test can hide an unverified production path.\n\n**How to verify.** Reproduce the dependency or hardware boundary, verify the gate is explicit and fail-closed, and identify the separate real integration job or evidence path that executes the contract.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Skipped or expected-failure test signal.\n\nWhy it matters: A conditional or ignored test can hide an unverified production path.\nHow to verify: Reproduce the dependency or hardware boundary, verify the gate is explicit and fail-closed, and identify the separate real integration job or evidence path that executes the contract."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta003-skip-or-xfail",
              "id": "TA003-skip-or-xfail",
