            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Coverage exclusions can conceal reachable error or integration paths."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Coverage exclusion signal in tracked Python or JavaScript-family text.\n\n**Why it matters.** Coverage exclusions can conceal reachable error or integration paths.\n\n**How to verify.** Prove the branch is structurally unreachable on every supported runtime or replace the exclusion with a real error-path or matrix test.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Coverage exclusion signal in tracked Python or JavaScript-family text.\n\nWhy it matters: Coverage exclusions can conceal reachable error or integration paths.\nHow to verify: Prove the branch is structurally unreachable on every supported runtime or replace the exclusion with a real error-path or matrix test."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta004-coverage-exclusion",
              "id": "TA004-coverage-exclusion",
