              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A type suppression can hide a broken production or test contract."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Local static-type suppression signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** A type suppression can hide a broken production or test contract.\n\n**How to verify.** Run strict typing on the owning module, confirm the exact error code and external typing boundary, then replace the suppression or document the narrow tracked reason.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Local static-type suppression signal.\n\nWhy it matters: A type suppression can hide a broken production or test contract.\nHow to verify: Run strict typing on the owning module, confirm the exact error code and external typing boundary, then replace the suppression or document the narrow tracked reason."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta006-type-suppression",
              "id": "TA006-type-suppression",
              "name": "TA006-type-suppression",
