              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Module injection can bypass import, packaging, or optional-dependency wiring."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Module-resolution injection signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** Module injection can bypass import, packaging, or optional-dependency wiring.\n\n**How to verify.** Execute the real package or direct-script import path in a clean subprocess and prove the same packaging and dependency boundary without replacing module resolution.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Module-resolution injection signal.\n\nWhy it matters: Module injection can bypass import, packaging, or optional-dependency wiring.\nHow to verify: Execute the real package or direct-script import path in a clean subprocess and prove the same packaging and dependency boundary without replacing module resolution."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ta007-module-injection",
              "id": "TA007-module-injection",
