            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The test owner name suggests a cross-module coverage bucket."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Non-specific test-owner name signal.\n\n**Why it matters.** The test owner name suggests a cross-module coverage bucket.\n\n**How to verify.** Map every test to one production module or one named integration contract and split unrelated behaviours into their owning test surfaces.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Non-specific test-owner name signal.\n\nWhy it matters: The test owner name suggests a cross-module coverage bucket.\nHow to verify: Map every test to one production module or one named integration contract and split unrelated behaviours into their owning test surfaces."
              },
