            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A first-party import cycle can invert ownership and obscure initialisation."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Non-trivial first-party Python import cycle.\n\n**Why it matters.** A first-party import cycle can invert ownership and obscure initialisation.\n\n**How to verify.** Trace runtime import order and public ownership for every edge; dismiss only if the cycle is type-only or otherwise absent from the production execution graph.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Non-trivial first-party Python import cycle.\n\nWhy it matters: A first-party import cycle can invert ownership and obscure initialisation.\nHow to verify: Trace runtime import order and public ownership for every edge; dismiss only if the cycle is type-only or otherwise absent from the production execution graph."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#ar001-first-party-import-cycle",
              "id": "AR001-first-party-import-cycle",
