            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A broad import guard can mask dependency defects as optional absence."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Import guarded by a broad exception handler.\n\n**Why it matters.** A broad import guard can mask dependency defects as optional absence.\n\n**How to verify.** Run the real import with the dependency present, absent, and broken inside its package; catch only the expected absence and surface nested failures.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Import guarded by a broad exception handler.\n\nWhy it matters: A broad import guard can mask dependency defects as optional absence.\nHow to verify: Run the real import with the dependency present, absent, and broken inside its package; catch only the expected absence and surface nested failures."
              },
