              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "eval and exec run arbitrary code and turn any tainted argument into execution."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Dynamic code execution through eval or exec.\n\n**Why it matters.** eval and exec run arbitrary code and turn any tainted argument into execution.\n\n**How to verify.** Trace the argument to a trusted literal or a validated allow-list; otherwise replace the call with an explicit parser, dispatch table, or sandboxed evaluator.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Dynamic code execution through eval or exec.\n\nWhy it matters: eval and exec run arbitrary code and turn any tainted argument into execution.\nHow to verify: Trace the argument to a trusted literal or a validated allow-list; otherwise replace the call with an explicit parser, dispatch table, or sandboxed evaluator."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as001-dynamic-code-execution",
              "id": "AS001-dynamic-code-execution",
