                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Dynamic code execution through eval or exec."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A shell command surface lets a tainted argument inject additional commands."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Shell command execution surface via shell=True, os.system, or os.popen.\n\n**Why it matters.** A shell command surface lets a tainted argument inject additional commands.\n\n**How to verify.** Pass an argument vector without a shell (shell=False, or subprocess with a list), or prove every interpolated value is a trusted constant.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Shell command execution surface via shell=True, os.system, or os.popen.\n\nWhy it matters: A shell command surface lets a tainted argument inject additional commands.\nHow to verify: Pass an argument vector without a shell (shell=False, or subprocess with a list), or prove every interpolated value is a trusted constant."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as002-shell-command-execution",
              "id": "AS002-shell-command-execution",
              "name": "AS002-shell-command-execution",
