              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Shell command execution surface via shell=True, os.system, or os.popen."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pickle and the default yaml.load reconstruct arbitrary objects from their input."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Unsafe deserialization via pickle or an unbounded yaml.load.\n\n**Why it matters.** pickle and the default yaml.load reconstruct arbitrary objects from their input.\n\n**How to verify.** Deserialize only trusted local data, or switch to a bounded safe format (yaml.safe_load, JSON, or a schema-validated parser) for any externally sourced bytes.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Unsafe deserialization via pickle or an unbounded yaml.load.\n\nWhy it matters: pickle and the default yaml.load reconstruct arbitrary objects from their input.\nHow to verify: Deserialize only trusted local data, or switch to a bounded safe format (yaml.safe_load, JSON, or a schema-validated parser) for any externally sourced bytes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as003-unsafe-deserialization",
              "id": "AS003-unsafe-deserialization",
