              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsafe deserialization via pickle or an unbounded yaml.load."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "md5 and sha1 are not collision resistant and must not back a security decision."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Weak hash primitive md5 or sha1 in a possible security context.\n\n**Why it matters.** md5 and sha1 are not collision resistant and must not back a security decision.\n\n**How to verify.** Confirm the digest is a non-security checksum; otherwise move to SHA-256 or a keyed MAC and record why the primitive is acceptable.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Weak hash primitive md5 or sha1 in a possible security context.\n\nWhy it matters: md5 and sha1 are not collision resistant and must not back a security decision.\nHow to verify: Confirm the digest is a non-security checksum; otherwise move to SHA-256 or a keyed MAC and record why the primitive is acceptable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as004-weak-hash-primitive",
              "id": "AS004-weak-hash-primitive",
