            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "eval and the Function constructor execute a string as code, turning any tainted argument into arbitrary execution."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native JavaScript or TypeScript dynamic code execution via eval or Function.\n\n**Why it matters.** eval and the Function constructor execute a string as code, turning any tainted argument into arbitrary execution.\n\n**How to verify.** Replace the dynamic evaluation with an explicit parser, a lookup table, or a typed dispatch; if evaluation is unavoidable, prove the source is a trusted literal.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native JavaScript or TypeScript dynamic code execution via eval or Function.\n\nWhy it matters: eval and the Function constructor execute a string as code, turning any tainted argument into arbitrary execution.\nHow to verify: Replace the dynamic evaluation with an explicit parser, a lookup table, or a typed dispatch; if evaluation is unavoidable, prove the source is a trusted literal."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as006-js-dynamic-code-execution",
