            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "os/exec runs an external command, so a tainted argument can execute an unintended program or, with a shell, inject further commands."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native Go external command execution via os/exec Command or CommandContext.\n\n**Why it matters.** os/exec runs an external command, so a tainted argument can execute an unintended program or, with a shell, inject further commands.\n\n**How to verify.** Prove every argument is a trusted constant or validated allow-list value, pass an explicit argument vector, and never build the command from unsanitised input.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native Go external command execution via os/exec Command or CommandContext.\n\nWhy it matters: os/exec runs an external command, so a tainted argument can execute an unintended program or, with a shell, inject further commands.\nHow to verify: Prove every argument is a trusted constant or validated allow-list value, pass an explicit argument vector, and never build the command from unsanitised input."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as007-go-command-execution",
              "id": "AS007-go-command-execution",
