              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An unsafe block suspends the compiler's memory-safety guarantees, so a mistake inside it can cause undefined behaviour that safe Rust would have prevented."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native Rust unsafe block that suspends compiler memory-safety guarantees.\n\n**Why it matters.** An unsafe block suspends the compiler's memory-safety guarantees, so a mistake inside it can cause undefined behaviour that safe Rust would have prevented.\n\n**How to verify.** Confirm the block is minimal, documents the invariants it upholds, and cannot be replaced by a safe abstraction; record why each unsafe operation is sound.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native Rust unsafe block that suspends compiler memory-safety guarantees.\n\nWhy it matters: An unsafe block suspends the compiler's memory-safety guarantees, so a mistake inside it can cause undefined behaviour that safe Rust would have prevented.\nHow to verify: Confirm the block is minimal, documents the invariants it upholds, and cannot be replaced by a safe abstraction; record why each unsafe operation is sound."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as008-rust-unsafe-block",
              "id": "AS008-rust-unsafe-block",
              "name": "AS008-rust-unsafe-block",
              "properties": {
                "category": "application-security",
                "introduced": "rigor-foundry/1.4.0",
                "tags": [
                  "rigor-foundry",
                  "application-security"
                ]
              },
              "relationships": [
