                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Native Rust unsafe block that suspends compiler memory-safety guarantees."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "gets, the unbounded str/sprintf family, and system/popen are classic buffer-overflow and command-injection surfaces when their input is not strictly bounded and trusted."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native C or C++ call to an unbounded or command-executing libc function.\n\n**Why it matters.** gets, the unbounded str/sprintf family, and system/popen are classic buffer-overflow and command-injection surfaces when their input is not strictly bounded and trusted.\n\n**How to verify.** Replace the call with a length-bounded equivalent (fgets, snprintf, strncpy with an explicit size) or an argument-vector exec, and prove the input is trusted and bounded.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native C or C++ call to an unbounded or command-executing libc function.\n\nWhy it matters: gets, the unbounded str/sprintf family, and system/popen are classic buffer-overflow and command-injection surfaces when their input is not strictly bounded and trusted.\nHow to verify: Replace the call with a length-bounded equivalent (fgets, snprintf, strncpy with an explicit size) or an argument-vector exec, and prove the input is trusted and bounded."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as009-c-unsafe-libc",
              "id": "AS009-c-unsafe-libc",
              "name": "AS009-c-unsafe-libc",
              "properties": {
                "category": "application-security",
                "introduced": "rigor-foundry/1.5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "rigor-foundry",
                  "application-security"
                ]
              },
              "relationships": [
