                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Native C or C++ call to an unbounded or command-executing libc function."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The unsafe_* intrinsics bypass Julia's bounds, type, and garbage-collection safety, so a bad pointer or length reads or writes arbitrary memory."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native Julia unsafe_* intrinsic that bypasses bounds, type, and GC safety.\n\n**Why it matters.** The unsafe_* intrinsics bypass Julia's bounds, type, and garbage-collection safety, so a bad pointer or length reads or writes arbitrary memory.\n\n**How to verify.** Confirm the pointer and length come from a live, correctly typed, GC-rooted object, or replace the intrinsic with a bounds-checked array or a safe wrapper.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native Julia unsafe_* intrinsic that bypasses bounds, type, and GC safety.\n\nWhy it matters: The unsafe_* intrinsics bypass Julia's bounds, type, and garbage-collection safety, so a bad pointer or length reads or writes arbitrary memory.\nHow to verify: Confirm the pointer and length come from a live, correctly typed, GC-rooted object, or replace the intrinsic with a bounds-checked array or a safe wrapper."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as010-julia-unsafe-memory",
              "id": "AS010-julia-unsafe-memory",
              "name": "AS010-julia-unsafe-memory",
