                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Native Julia unsafe_* intrinsic that bypasses bounds, type, and GC safety."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The shell eval builtin re-parses and executes its argument as a command, so any tainted value in that argument becomes an injected command."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Native shell eval builtin that re-parses its argument as a command.\n\n**Why it matters.** The shell eval builtin re-parses and executes its argument as a command, so any tainted value in that argument becomes an injected command.\n\n**How to verify.** Remove eval and call the command with an explicit argument vector, or prove every interpolated value is a trusted constant.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Native shell eval builtin that re-parses its argument as a command.\n\nWhy it matters: The shell eval builtin re-parses and executes its argument as a command, so any tainted value in that argument becomes an injected command.\nHow to verify: Remove eval and call the command with an explicit argument vector, or prove every interpolated value is a trusted constant."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#as011-shell-eval-execution",
              "id": "AS011-shell-eval-execution",
