            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A mutable default argument is created once and shared across every call, so state leaks between invocations."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Mutable default argument shared across calls, leaking state between invocations.\n\n**Why it matters.** A mutable default argument is created once and shared across every call, so state leaks between invocations.\n\n**How to verify.** Default the parameter to None and create the list, dict, or set inside the function body, or confirm the shared instance is genuinely intended.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Mutable default argument shared across calls, leaking state between invocations.\n\nWhy it matters: A mutable default argument is created once and shared across every call, so state leaks between invocations.\nHow to verify: Default the parameter to None and create the list, dict, or set inside the function body, or confirm the shared instance is genuinely intended."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#rl002-mutable-default-argument",
              "id": "RL002-mutable-default-argument",
