              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Mutable default argument shared across calls, leaking state between invocations."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A hash-pinned lock file records integrity digests for every dependency, but this pinned requirement carries none, so its artefact is installed without verification against tampering or index substitution."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Pinned requirement in a hash-mode lock file carries no integrity hash.\n\n**Why it matters.** A hash-pinned lock file records integrity digests for every dependency, but this pinned requirement carries none, so its artefact is installed without verification against tampering or index substitution.\n\n**How to verify.** Recompile the lock with hashes (for example `pip-compile --generate-hashes`) so every pinned requirement carries a `--hash=` digest, or justify why this dependency is exempt.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Pinned requirement in a hash-mode lock file carries no integrity hash.\n\nWhy it matters: A hash-pinned lock file records integrity digests for every dependency, but this pinned requirement carries none, so its artefact is installed without verification against tampering or index substitution.\nHow to verify: Recompile the lock with hashes (for example `pip-compile --generate-hashes`) so every pinned requirement carries a `--hash=` digest, or justify why this dependency is exempt."
              },
