            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A base image referenced only by tag is mutable, so the resolved image can change under the same Dockerfile and is never verified against a known digest."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Dockerfile base image referenced by a mutable tag with no immutable digest.\n\n**Why it matters.** A base image referenced only by tag is mutable, so the resolved image can change under the same Dockerfile and is never verified against a known digest.\n\n**How to verify.** Pin the base image to an immutable `@sha256:` digest (for example `python:3.12-slim@sha256:...`), or justify why a moving tag is required.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Dockerfile base image referenced by a mutable tag with no immutable digest.\n\nWhy it matters: A base image referenced only by tag is mutable, so the resolved image can change under the same Dockerfile and is never verified against a known digest.\nHow to verify: Pin the base image to an immutable `@sha256:` digest (for example `python:3.12-slim@sha256:...`), or justify why a moving tag is required."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#dk001-unpinned-base-image",
              "id": "DK001-unpinned-base-image",
