            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The final image stage sets no non-root USER, so the container runs as root and a process escape keeps full root authority inside the namespace."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Dockerfile runtime stage sets no non-root USER, so the container runs as root.\n\n**Why it matters.** The final image stage sets no non-root USER, so the container runs as root and a process escape keeps full root authority inside the namespace.\n\n**How to verify.** Add a `USER` directive selecting an unprivileged account (and create it if needed) as the last identity in the runtime stage, or justify the root run.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Dockerfile runtime stage sets no non-root USER, so the container runs as root.\n\nWhy it matters: The final image stage sets no non-root USER, so the container runs as root and a process escape keeps full root authority inside the namespace.\nHow to verify: Add a `USER` directive selecting an unprivileged account (and create it if needed) as the last identity in the runtime stage, or justify the root run."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#dk002-root-runtime-user",
              "id": "DK002-root-runtime-user",
