            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A credential-named variable is assigned a string literal, so a secret is embedded in tracked source where it cannot be rotated and is exposed to everyone with repository read access."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Credential-named variable assigned a string literal secret in tracked source.\n\n**Why it matters.** A credential-named variable is assigned a string literal, so a secret is embedded in tracked source where it cannot be rotated and is exposed to everyone with repository read access.\n\n**How to verify.** Load the value from an environment variable or secret manager at runtime and remove the literal, or confirm it is a non-secret placeholder or fixture.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Credential-named variable assigned a string literal secret in tracked source.\n\nWhy it matters: A credential-named variable is assigned a string literal, so a secret is embedded in tracked source where it cannot be rotated and is exposed to everyone with repository read access.\nHow to verify: Load the value from an environment variable or secret manager at runtime and remove the literal, or confirm it is a non-secret placeholder or fixture."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#dp001-hardcoded-credential",
              "id": "DP001-hardcoded-credential",
