              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A test compares a direct floating-point literal with exact equality, which can hide representation or tolerance assumptions."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Python test uses exact equality against a direct floating-point literal.\n\n**Why it matters.** A test compares a direct floating-point literal with exact equality, which can hide representation or tolerance assumptions.\n\n**How to verify.** Use a justified absolute/relative tolerance or prove exact binary identity is intended.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Python test uses exact equality against a direct floating-point literal.\n\nWhy it matters: A test compares a direct floating-point literal with exact equality, which can hide representation or tolerance assumptions.\nHow to verify: Use a justified absolute/relative tolerance or prove exact binary identity is intended."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#sn001-exact-float-equality-in-test",
