              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A supported stochastic API is used before deterministic local seeding, so repeated test outcomes may consume different samples."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Python test uses a supported stochastic API before deterministic local seeding.\n\n**Why it matters.** A supported stochastic API is used before deterministic local seeding, so repeated test outcomes may consume different samples.\n\n**How to verify.** Seed before the first draw or construct the local generator with a seed, then verify deterministic replay.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Python test uses a supported stochastic API before deterministic local seeding.\n\nWhy it matters: A supported stochastic API is used before deterministic local seeding, so repeated test outcomes may consume different samples.\nHow to verify: Seed before the first draw or construct the local generator with a seed, then verify deterministic replay."
              },
