            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Library code writes directly to process output, bypassing caller-controlled observability and output routing."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Python library code calls builtin print outside an intentional command surface.\n\n**Why it matters.** Library code writes directly to process output, bypassing caller-controlled observability and output routing.\n\n**How to verify.** Replace incidental output with a returned value or structured logger, or prove the module is an intentional command boundary.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Python library code calls builtin print outside an intentional command surface.\n\nWhy it matters: Library code writes directly to process output, bypassing caller-controlled observability and output routing.\nHow to verify: Replace incidental output with a returned value or structured logger, or prove the module is an intentional command boundary."
              },
