            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A test assertion reads a process wall clock without a recognised local freeze or dominating monkeypatch, so scheduling and clock movement can change its result."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Python test assertion reads an imported wall clock without explicit local control.\n\n**Why it matters.** A test assertion reads a process wall clock without a recognised local freeze or dominating monkeypatch, so scheduling and clock movement can change its result.\n\n**How to verify.** Inject or freeze the clock at the assertion boundary, then replay the test with the exact controlled timestamp; retain a live-clock assertion only with bounded timing evidence and an explicit review.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Python test assertion reads an imported wall clock without explicit local control.\n\nWhy it matters: A test assertion reads a process wall clock without a recognised local freeze or dominating monkeypatch, so scheduling and clock movement can change its result.\nHow to verify: Inject or freeze the clock at the assertion boundary, then replay the test with the exact controlled timestamp; retain a live-clock assertion only with bounded timing evidence and an explicit review."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#pr001-wall-clock-in-test",
