            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A declared Python public surface is not bound exactly by the tracked API manifest, so compatibility review cannot distinguish an intentional API edit from drift. The tracked public API manifest is malformed or retains a surface with no matching literal declaration, so it cannot bind the repository's declared API state."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Declared Python public surface differs from its tracked pinned manifest.\n\n**When the declared public surface is not bound by the manifest.**\n\n**Why it matters.** A declared Python public surface is not bound exactly by the tracked API manifest, so compatibility review cannot distinguish an intentional API edit from drift.\n\n**How to verify.** Review the declared names and downstream compatibility contract, then update rigor-public-api.json only when the exact public-surface change is intentional; do not infer a breaking change from unrelated source edits.\n\n**When the manifest is malformed or records a surface with no declaration.**\n\n**Why it matters.** The tracked public API manifest is malformed or retains a surface with no matching literal declaration, so it cannot bind the repository's declared API state.\n\n**How to verify.** Validate the versioned manifest schema and compare every recorded path with its exact module-level __all__; remove or update a row only after compatibility review.\n\nA RigorFoundry result is an audit candidate for evidence review, never a defect verdict; only a validated review record decides it.",
                "text": "Declared Python public surface differs from its tracked pinned manifest.\n\nWhen the declared public surface is not bound by the manifest:\nWhy it matters: A declared Python public surface is not bound exactly by the tracked API manifest, so compatibility review cannot distinguish an intentional API edit from drift.\nHow to verify: Review the declared names and downstream compatibility contract, then update rigor-public-api.json only when the exact public-surface change is intentional; do not infer a breaking change from unrelated source edits.\n\nWhen the manifest is malformed or records a surface with no declaration:\nWhy it matters: The tracked public API manifest is malformed or retains a surface with no matching literal declaration, so it cannot bind the repository's declared API state.\nHow to verify: Validate the versioned manifest schema and compare every recorded path with its exact module-level __all__; remove or update a row only after compatibility review."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anulum/RIGOR-FOUNDRY/blob/main/docs/rule-catalogue.md#aa001-unbound-api-manifest",
              "id": "AA001-unbound-api-manifest",
              "name": "AA001-unbound-api-manifest",
              "properties": {
                "category": "api-compatibility",
                "introduced": "rigor-foundry/1.16.0",
                "tags": [
                  "rigor-foundry",
                  "api-compatibility"
                ]
              },
